WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:06.170
The cold isolation of space. Nowhere to run
and nowhere to hide. Aliens stalk the halls

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:12.579
with only one thing on their minds: expand
and consume. Keep watching to see how each

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.400
Alien movie connects to one another!

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.730
In the late 1970s, H. R. Giger designed a
new horrific movie monster: the Xenomorph.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:26.490
It became iconic for its lethal serrated tail,
its flesh-tearing proboscis, and acidic blood

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.390
that could burn through the hull of a spaceship.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:34.399
Director Ridley Scott took Giger's creature
and placed it inside the Nostromo, a futuristic

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:38.490
yet claustrophobic spaceship that becomes
little more than a tomb for the Xenomorph's

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:45.199
many victims. Upon its 1979 premiere, Alien
cemented itself as a sci-fi horror phenomenon,

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:49.430
with Sigourney Weaver's Ellen Ripley enduring
as one of the most iconic protagonists in

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:51.060
cinematic history.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:55.370
In the years since, the Alien universe has
developed a massive legacy steeped in expansive

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.370
lore.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:01.740
"I think they want us to come and find them."

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.580
While Prometheus was also helmed by Scott,
this prequel was a markedly different experience

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.552
than the original movie. The film follows
Dr. Elizabeth Shaw — played by Noomi Rapace

00:01:11.552 --> 00:01:16.790
— and Dr. Charlie Holloway — portrayed
by Logan Marshall-Green — as they try to

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:20.150
answer humanity's big question: "Where do
we come from?"

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:25.110
The two archeologists discover evidence across
multiple cultures and time periods suggesting

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:30.570
that humans worshiped giant mysterious beings.
This evidence also suggests an unknown importance

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:36.420
surrounding the distant moon, LV-223. Funded
by the Weyland Corporation, the pair embark

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:41.140
on a two-year journey into space aboard the
starship, Prometheus. The crew is eventually

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.860
awakened from stasis by the android David
— played by Michael Fassbender.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:51.710
Upon landing, they discover impressive technology
years beyond humanity, along with vases of

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:56.170
dark, unidentified goo. While studying what
they've found, several crew members are attacked

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:02.120
and infected by alien lifeforms. Simultaneously,
David experiments on other crew members using

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:06.250
the newfound goo. But the real kicker comes
from the head of one of those large humanoid

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.649
beings depicted on Earth. The species is given
the moniker, "the engineers."

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.299
After doctors Holloway and Shaw are intimate
with one another, they come to realize Holloway

00:02:16.299 --> 00:02:21.000
is infected with an alien contagion, leading
to his premature death at the hands of the

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.000
crew.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.540
Still reeling from Holloway's demise, the
crew soon discovers they've been transporting

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.239
the withered Peter Weyland — played by Guy
Pearce — so that he could discover the key

00:02:29.239 --> 00:02:34.560
to immortality. To this end, Weyland and David
locate a living engineer in stasis and awaken

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.260
it. While Weyland is convinced the engineer
species were the original creators of humanity

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:44.220
and his source of salvation, the engineer
ultimately kills him, decapitates David, and

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.620
is hellbent on tracking down the remaining
crew.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.310
Dr. Shaw learns that she is pregnant with
an alien lifeform and manages to extract the

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:56.200
octopus-like creature from her abdomen. Through
this, she deduces that the goo found on the

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:01.730
moon was created by the engineers to wipe
out humanity. After Shaw bests the engineer,

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:06.879
she takes David's still-active head and commandeers
a ship to find the engineers' homeworld. As

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:10.920
Prometheus concludes, the octopus-like monster,
which Shaw had unleashed on the engineer to

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:16.519
provide her escape, is revealed to be a proto-facehugger.
It implants the engineer with a chest-bursting

00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:21.080
embryo similar to the Xenomorphs, setting
the stage for the rest of the franchise.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:27.999
"They are a dying species, grasping for resurrection.
They don't deserve to start again, and I'm

00:03:27.999 --> 00:03:28.999
not going to let them."

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:35.150
Nearly 11 years after the events of Prometheus,
a solar flare damages the colonization ship

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:40.150
Covenant while it's en route to its designated
planet. The android Walter, played by Michael

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:45.349
Fassbender, awakens the emergency crew, only
to have their captain perish due to a technical

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:50.400
malfunction. Upon repairing the ship, the
Covenant crew receives a mysterious transmission,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:56.080
which they trace back to a nearby planet.
This setup kicks off 2017's Alien: Covenant,

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.550
Scott's second prequel.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:01.919
The acting captain Christopher Oram — played
by Billy Crudup — decides to settle on this

00:04:01.919 --> 00:04:06.849
new planet instead. While receiving pushback
from Chief Katherine Daniels — portrayed

00:04:06.849 --> 00:04:11.583
by Katherine Waterston — Oram steers the
Covenant towards the signal. They discover

00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:16.630
the engineer ship, which Dr. Shaw had stolen
in the final act of Prometheus, and after

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:21.200
trekking through the planet's wilderness,
two of the crew are infected by airborne spores.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:26.600
The spores gestate into the newly dubbed Neomorphs,
which quickly grow into adulthood and attack

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:31.460
the crew. Amid the chaos, the Prometheus android
David comes to their rescue.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:36.810
While the crew is initially trusting, they
realize David has grown a god-complex through

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:41.450
his years in isolation. It's revealed that
he killed Dr. Shaw to experiment on her and

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:45.940
systematically wiped the engineer species
from their homeworld using the bio-agent that

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:50.200
had been developed to kill humanity. Not only
that, but David was the one who engineered

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.920
the genetic make-up of what would become the
Xenomorph.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:58.390
As Oram is infected by a facehugger, the remaining
crew make moves to immediately leave the planet.

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:02.560
But when David destroys Walter and boards
the Covenant posing as him, he's followed

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:06.320
by two Xenomorphs, who resume terrorizing
the crew.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.660
After the Xenomorphs are destroyed, the remaining
crew enter hypersleep to continue their journey

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:15.570
to their original destination. But as Katherine
enters her pod, she realizes in horror that

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:20.840
David has replaced Walter and is now in control
of the ship. While she falls into stasis,

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:25.720
we see David placing the Xenomorph embryos
in c old storage, setting up some of the groundwork

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.890
for the original 1979 film.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:34.920
"This is Ripley. Last survivor of the Nostromo.
Signing off."

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:41.990
Alien takes place 17 years after Alien: Covenant.
In the original, landmark flick, we are introduced

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:46.940
to the crew of the Nostromo as they come across
a wayward distress signal. Captain Dallas

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:51.141
— played by Tom Skerritt — decides to
investigate, and the crew discovers an alien

00:05:51.141 --> 00:05:56.690
ship bearing a dead engineer and several alien
eggs. After a facehugger emerges and attaches

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:01.090
itself to Kane — portrayed by John Hurt
— they break quarantine procedures and bring

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:04.300
their affected teammate back aboard the Nostromo.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.310
While the film chronology confirms this as
an engineer ship, the fact that the android

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:12.960
David was the final designer of the Xenomorph
species leads to narrative inconsistencies.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.470
For the time between the end of Alien: Covenant
and the start of the original movie, there

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:22.330
are no explanations as to how another engineer
ship came to contain a species that wasn't

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:28.220
created by them. With an Alien TV series reportedly
on the way and Ridley Scott indicating another

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:32.350
film is in the works, it's possible this gap
will be bridged in future installments.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:38.480
While the crew fails to safely remove the
facehugger from Kane, it implants a Xenomorph

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:42.490
embryo down his gullet. After he wakes and
joins his shipmates for a meal, the hidden

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:47.460
parasite bursts from his chest cavity, shocking
the rest of the crew before scurrying off.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:51.380
As they hunt for the creature, it grows rapidly
and starts picking off members of the team

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:52.520
one by one.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:56.700
The science officer Ash — played by Ian
Holm — is discovered to be an android tasked

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:01.460
with the preservation of the Xenomorph for
further study, regardless of the human passengers’

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:06.540
safety. After Ripley sets the ship to self-destruct
and flees in an escape pod, she has one final

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:11.470
showdown with the Xenomorph, which ends in
her blasting it into space using the pod’s

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:16.160
exhaust. From there, she sets a course for
Earth and falls back into hypersleep.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.260
Alien's major conflict has less to do with
the deadly alien aboard the Nostromo and more

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:25.150
to do with a shadowy corporation using whatever
means to achieve their goals. However, exactly

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:29.830
how The Weyland Corporation discovered the
Xenomorph's location prior to our main cast

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:32.200
finding the derelict ship remains a mystery.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:37.861
"Ma'am, I already said that it was not indigenous.
It was a derelict spacecraft. It was an alien

00:07:37.861 --> 00:07:39.450
ship. It was not from there."

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:44.710
At the start of James Cameron's sequel Aliens,
Ripley wakes up on a space station orbiting

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:51.170
Earth after 57 years in stasis. She is debriefed
by the Weyland-Yutani Corporation, who abjectly

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:55.710
dismiss her explanation of what happened in
the previous movie. However, the Weyland-Yutani

00:07:55.710 --> 00:08:00.090
representative Carter Burke — played by
Paul Reiser — informs Ripley that they lost

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:04.690
contact with the terraforming colony, Hadley's
Hope. He convinces her to join a mission in

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:09.300
which they will determine the colony's fate,
as well as destroy any alien species alive

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.440
on the planet.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:15.390
Upon their arrival, the Colonial Marines discover
a young girl named Newt — portrayed by Carrie

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:20.450
Henn — and the rest of the population cocooned
in unrecognizable goo. With chestbursters

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:25.310
popping from these trapped victims and adult
aliens attacking the team, Ripley realizes

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:30.130
that the Xenomorphs are using humans as incubators.
As attacks continue, the question becomes:

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.550
How are the eggs being created?

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:36.159
Ripley soon uncovers how Burke had ordered
the colonists to investigate the derelict

00:08:36.159 --> 00:08:41.319
engineer ship still in orbit so that Weyland-Yutani
could use the species for weapons research.

00:08:41.319 --> 00:08:46.199
Ultimately, Ripley, Newt, the android Bishop
— played by Lance Henriksen — and Corporal

00:08:46.199 --> 00:08:49.649
Hicks — portrayed by Michael Biehn — are
the only survivors.

00:08:49.649 --> 00:08:53.970
The aliens target Newt after she is separated
from Ripley, who then pursues them into the

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:58.500
heart of their hive and finds the Xenomorph
queen. After reclaiming Newt and escaping

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:02.649
the queen, they board a ship to leave the
planetoid behind. But the queen manages to

00:09:02.649 --> 00:09:07.790
get aboard. Ripley battles the monster via
a mechanical ExoSuit and forces it out of

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:12.779
an airlock. The survivors then enter hypersleep
for a trip back to Earth and credits roll.

00:09:12.779 --> 00:09:19.100
"This is Ripley. Last survivor of the Nostromo.
Signing off."

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:26.550
David Fincher's 1992 film Alien 3 begins directly
after the events of the previous installment.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:31.010
A mysterious fire on Ripley's ship forces
the computer to launch its escape pods onto

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:36.900
the planet Fiorina 161. After Ripley is recovered
by Doctor Clemens — played by Charles Dance

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:41.519
— she is brought to an all-male maximum-security
prison. She learns that Newt and Hicks were

00:09:41.519 --> 00:09:45.970
killed in the spaceship crash, while also
being informed that a message was sent to

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:48.290
Weyland-Yutani for them to come and collect
her.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:52.850
Uncertain of what caused the fire on her ship,
Ripley convinces Clemens to autopsy Newt's

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:58.120
body. However, when a prison inmate dies under
strange circumstances, she suspects that another

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:01.749
Xenomorph managed to board her ship and is
now loose in the prison.

00:10:01.749 --> 00:10:06.399
When Ripley finds and reactivates Bishop,
he confirms her fears of a rogue Xenomorph

00:10:06.399 --> 00:10:10.860
just as it ramps up its attacks on inmates.
But since the prison lacks any kind of weapons

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:14.779
stockpile, the remaining prisoners must lure
the alien into a death trap.

00:10:14.779 --> 00:10:18.920
As they work to put their plan into motion,
Ripley finds out that she is the current incubator

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:23.890
for a new Xenomorph queen. She realizes she
must kill herself, but not before helping

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:28.310
the prison crew stop the alien. Knowing it
won't hurt her because she's pregnant, Ripley

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:32.680
and the remaining crew corner the alien, dump
molten lead on it, cool it with the emergency

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:35.980
sprinkler system, and shatter the creature
to pieces.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:40.079
Upon their victory, however, Weyland-Yutani
arrives. They try to convince Ripley that

00:10:40.079 --> 00:10:44.140
they can safely remove the gestating queen
from her body, but she doesn't buy it for

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:50.810
an instant. She jumps into a massive blast
furnace, killing herself and the queen. Or,

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:54.060
so it seemed.

00:10:55.149 --> 00:11:01.529
Jean-Pierre Jeunet's 1997 follow-up Alien:
Resurrection depicts the final chronological

00:11:01.529 --> 00:11:06.999
events in the Alien film saga, especially
since Ridley Scott declared the Alien Vs Predator

00:11:06.999 --> 00:11:11.990
movies non-canonical. This installment, originally
penned by Joss Whedon, takes the Jurassic

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:16.509
World approach to its story. It depicts the
United Systems' ill-advised attempt to clone

00:11:16.509 --> 00:11:20.319
the Xenomorphs some 200 years after the events
of Alien 3.

00:11:20.319 --> 00:11:26.129
Utilizing Ripley's DNA, the USM creates clones
of her with the alien queen embryo still inside.

00:11:26.129 --> 00:11:30.730
Following seven unsuccessful attempts, they
finally create Ripley 8, who possesses the

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:35.420
original Ellen Ripley's genetic memories.
Additionally, since her DNA was grafted with

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:40.370
that of the Xenomorph queen, the queen also
shares the same genetic knowledge as her host,

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:42.610
making them both partial hybrids of each other.

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:47.509
When a rag-tag mercenary ship called the Betty
arrives and delivers humans to serve as hosts

00:11:47.509 --> 00:11:51.720
for alien embryos, you can almost hear Ian
Malcolm's voice in Jurassic Park stammering

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:56.720
that life will find a way. While these human
sacrifices do indeed produce aliens, the newer

00:11:56.720 --> 00:12:00.439
spawns use their new genetic knowledge to
break free of their containment.

00:12:00.439 --> 00:12:04.649
The aliens proceed to attack the remaining
soldiers left onboard, and after a burst of

00:12:04.649 --> 00:12:09.320
bloody mayhem, only a few survivors remain.
By this point, Ripley 8 has discovered her

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:13.829
own superhuman strength and acidic blood.
In the meantime, the survivors find out the

00:12:13.829 --> 00:12:18.600
station is on autopilot and heading for Earth.
Seeing the looming catastrophe in front of

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:23.500
them, the team moves to escape via the Betty
and destroy the USM station. But before they

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:28.160
can all get to their liferaft, Ripley 8 is
abducted by a Xenomorph and taken back to

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.079
the hive. It's revealed to her that the alien
queen has evolved to possess a human-like

00:12:32.079 --> 00:12:36.970
reproductive system, and she gives birth to
a fully-fledged human-alien hybrid.

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:41.019
When Ripley 8 manages to escape the Xenomorph
swarm and boards the Betty with the rest of

00:12:41.019 --> 00:12:45.750
the crew, an open hatch prevents them from
leaving. As they move to fix the issue, the

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:50.180
human-alien hybrid attacks. Ripley 8 stops
the creature by using its genetic trust in

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:55.079
her against it. While hugging the hybrid,
she creates a hole in a nearby window using

00:12:55.079 --> 00:12:59.649
her acid blood, which violently sucks the
creature into space. The movie concludes with

00:12:59.649 --> 00:13:04.430
the remaining crew arriving on Earth, optimistic
for a future without the threat of a Xenomorph

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.819
apocalypse. Well, at least for now.

00:13:07.819 --> 00:13:12.129
